WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.867
Here we calculate length of stay PostgreSQL allows
us to subtract

00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:08.779
one date from another to get the number of days
between them

00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:14.876
But first we define the population We only want
completed stays so

00:00:14.902 --> 00:00:19.686
the WHERE clause removes records where the discharge
date is null Then

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:24.920
the case expression categorizes the calculated stay
Less than five days is

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:30.229
Short Five through ten days is Medium More than ten
days is

00:00:30.255 --> 00:00:33.760
Long Run the code in the browser and look at both
the

00:00:33.786 --> 00:00:39.321
calculated number of days and the final category You
can also copy

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:44.027
the query into pgAdmin This is a good example of
separating two

00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:48.614
questions first which records belong in the analysis
and second how should

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.547
the included records be classified
